glossary:
  - term: Shatt al-Arab
    gloss: The single river formed where the Tigris joins the Euphrates near
      al-Qurnah, and which runs on to the Persian Gulf.
  - term: Distributary channel
    gloss: A branch that carries water away from a river instead of into it; the
      Tigris throws off several near its confluence, feeding the Central and
      Hawizeh Marshes.
  - term: Silt
    gloss: The sediment a slow river drops as it goes; the Euphrates deposited
      more of it than the Tigris and built up a higher bed.
  - term: Idigna / Idiqlat
    gloss: The Sumerian and Akkadian names of the river, the Sumerian
      interpretable as "the swift river".
  - term: Aranzah
    gloss: "The Hurrian name of the Tigris, deified as a god: son of Kumarbi,
      brother of Teshub and Tašmišu."
  - term: Masbuta
    gloss: The baptism for which the Mandaeans use the water of the Tigris.
  - term: Affluence
    gloss: A stream feeding the river; the Tigris takes in Garzan, Anbarçayi,
      Batman, and the Great and Little Zab.
further:
