    why: The other of the two great rivers that define Mesopotamia, and the slow
      one the Tigris was named against.
  - slug: assyria
    why: The empire the Tigris nurtured, which left remnants along the river such
      as the relief of King Tiglath-Pileser.
  - slug: lagash
    why: A city irrigated by the Tigris through a canal dug around 2900 B.C.
